      "provenance": {
        "notes": "A cool, dry winter rest of one to two months (NC State: nights under 50 F; RHS: cooler, drier winter) is needed to flower; no page gives a watering number for it, so the rest factor is unknown. Likes to be rootbound (NC State, RHS). Watering: NC State drought tolerant, overwatering rots the crown; RHS dislikes soggy compost, water freely in summer; mapped to let_top_dry (agent). Light: RHS filtered or indirect, scorches in direct sun; NC State morning sun is best as a houseplant (stored the shadier reading). Size: NC State 2 ft tall by 3 ft wide, RHS 10 to 50 cm; NC State figures stored. Habit: basal strap-like leaves in a clump, no stem; 'rosette' is the agent's mapping. Toxicity: ASPCA (lycorine and other alkaloids; vomiting, drooling, diarrhoea; large amounts convulsions, low blood pressure, tremors, heart rhythm changes; bulbs worst) says toxic to dogs and cats; NC State rates humans low severity with the same signs and says no contact dermatitis. Pets graded 2 because of the heart and nerve effects after large doses; the grade is the agent's. The RHS page read says nothing on toxicity."
      },
